{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"4f89a647f705876b69915e05cdf76bc13ddb04452f3291305f41a7f8afa15f39","digest":{"component_or_area":"grounding coverage reconstruction tests","key_entities":["test_full_backend_account_is_present","test_metric_backend_skip_is_reconstructable","_METRIC_CANDIDATES","_resolve_binary","_metric_invoke","tests/unit/grounding/test_coverage_reconstruction.py","src/rebar/grounding/engine_b_backends.py"],"problem_keywords":["test flakiness","host-dependent test","metric tool detection","coverage reconstruction","fixture control"],"propositions":["test_full_backend_account_is_present fails deterministically on hosts with scc or lizard installed because it does not control _METRIC_CANDIDATES availability, leaving the test host-dependent","the test fixture is below the 800-LOC metric threshold, so when scc/lizard is present on PATH, _metric_invoke returns no match and emits no metric coverage record","test_metric_backend_skip_is_reconstructable already uses explicit missing-metric-tool fixture control to force skipped coverage reconstruction; test_full_backend_account_is_present requires the same control for parity","the fix adds _METRIC_CANDIDATES fixture control to force missing metric tool and asserts skipped coverage with reason=no_tool, without changing production grounding or evidence schema semantics"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787402973069079001,"uuid":"76fa3aeb-3ff0-4d80-ba70-091a4ec4f2d8"}